1
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:27,037
This is the fastest way to fish,

2
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:29,917
I'm sure your parents will be happy
that tonight's dinner is taken care of.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,480
You think so?

4
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:37,520
But I can't control my strength, so
I'm always breaking stuff at home.

5
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:42,880
And because of that, Mom and Dad get so
embarrassed that they can't help but laugh.

6
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:45,840
Hey, you gotta look up.

7
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,137
Otherwise you can't choose a product.

8
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,340
What product?

9
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:05,160
Where did this big, medley box come from?

10
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:09,000
For some reason, it feels familiar.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,647
Something tells me that this box
is friendly and kind-hearted.

12
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,680
Right, this magic item saved my life.

13
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,664
He's a precious friend of mine.

14
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:20,940
Don't go, Boxo.

15
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,960
Please take me with you.

16
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:24,904
Don't leave me all alone again.

17
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:29,740
After you got abducted, she was so
frantic she didn't even stop to sleep.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,360
I didn't know that.

19
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:35,217
I think this might have
reminded her of an old incident.

20
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,130
Old incident?

21
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,626
It's probably alright
for me to tell you this.

22
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:44,599
You see, years ago our village was
wiped out during a monster attack.

23
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,560
It was awful.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,412
Lamas and I were among the few survivors.

25
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,659
Both of our parents ended up dying.

26
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:56,451
Lamas had her blessing then,
but she was too scared to act.

27
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:01,546
That's why, to this day, she blames herself
for not being able to save everyone.

28
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:05,842
I remember she used to be too
afraid to even kill the tiniest bug.

29
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,908
And now she's become a
hunter of all things.

30
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,813
I had no idea she went through all that.

31
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:18,044
If there's anything that I can do
to help her out, I have to try.

32
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:19,880
Hey, Boxo?

33
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:23,160
Promise me, we'll always be together.

34
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,260
Of course.

35
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:28,409
I'll be here for as
long as you'll have me.

36
00:02:58,280 --> 00:02:59,110
believe

37
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:16,483
and I'm not alone.

38
00:03:16,566 --> 00:03:17,396
It's your memory, and you
can't find a special moment,

39
00:03:17,479 --> 00:03:18,309
but in the meantime, there are
no friends we haven't seen.

40
00:03:18,392 --> 00:03:19,417
It's amazing how I can see
it, and why are you there?

41
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,717
It's amazing that I can't see it.

42
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,271
I'm still waiting for it.

43
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:42,340
Thank you.

44
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:06,834
I've decided to stay in this
village for a little while.

45
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,745
Looks like we'll be neighbors.

46
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:09,810
Hello there.

47
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:14,377
If you have any questions about how
things work here, feel free to ask.

48
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,440
Sure, I'll be counting on you.

49
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:21,197
Great, Director Bear asked me to help
with some more reconstruction around town.

50
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:24,340
I'll see you later. No
problem. Have fun, I guess.

51
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,740
Miss Hulemy, Mr.

52
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:32,380
Boxo, we need a favor.

53
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:36,136
Aren't these guys Suori's bodyguards?

54
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,340
What's going on?

55
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:38,921
Later today, Mr.

56
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:42,197
Suori intends to approach the two
of you with a personal request.

57
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:45,657
We'd like to ask that you hear
what she has to say and then agree.

58
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:46,570
Wait a second.

59
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:50,544
You want us to say yes before we
even know what she's asking for?

60
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:54,135
What do you mean she's already nearby?

61
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,817
Please keep our conversation a secret.

62
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,841
She'd skin us alive if she
found out we were here.

63
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:01,100
Hey, seriously?

64
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,980
Um, excuse me?

65
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:08,160
Are you the famous magic
item engineer, Hulemy?

66
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,717
Sorry, I didn't mean to interrupt you.

67
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,153
Yeah, that would be me.

68
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:13,580
What's your name?

69
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:14,910
You may...

70
00:05:14,993 --> 00:05:17,300
I mean, my name is Suori.

71
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:22,117
Please forgive my rudeness, but I have
a matter I need your help dealing with.

72
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,030
Stand up.

73
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:25,637
You don't have to do
stuff like that, okay?

74
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:28,120
Enough with the bowing. Oh, yes.

75
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,277
Does that mean you'll accept my request?

76
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:34,720
I didn't say that, but if you
tell me more, I will consider it.

77
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:39,276
Very soon, there's going to
be an important gathering.

78
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,397
Influential merchant
families will be showing off

79
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,077
their magic items and
engineers and their employee.

80
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:47,217
Ah, that explains why you
had your eye on me and Boxxo.

81
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,130
Yes.

82
00:05:48,213 --> 00:05:50,217
I know the girl who planned the event.

83
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:54,897
Her name is Kanashi, and she's from a
rival merchant family with ties to my own.

84
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:58,862
Just the thought of her annoying
face is enough to make me scream!

85
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,147
I guess even rich people
have their problems.

86
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,480
Well, it sounds fun.

87
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,249
I could get down to party.

88
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:11,120
What do you think, Boxo? Hello there!

89
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,445
I guess that decides it, then.

90
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:14,880
Thank you very much!

91
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:23,231
Do you have a clear view back there, Boxo?

92
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:24,300
Hello there!

93
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:28,980
By the way, where's this girl Suwori
has such a huge grudge against?

94
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:32,260
From the sounds of it, they
should be close in age.

95
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,640
Ah, there she is.

96
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:38,557
In terms of who pulls off the
rich girl look, she might win out.

97
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,520
Miss Kanashi!

98
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,660
It's been far too long.

99
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:44,440
How nice to see you, Miss Suwori.

100
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,217
Please don't feel any
need to put yourself out.

101
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:49,717
It might be best if
you take your seat now.

102
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:53,817
That way you'll have the perfect view
from which to watch the proceedings.

103
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:56,665
You needn't try so hard
yourself, Miss Kanashi.

104
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:59,457
I'm afraid my conscience
wouldn't be able to handle it

105
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:02,097
if your little black heart
were to give up from shock.

106
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,140
Is that so?

107
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,692
I wasn't aware you even had a conscience.

108
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:09,577
It seems your hearing is as
awful as your personality.

109
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,240
Oh, I pity you, my dear.

110
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:15,120
This is way too mean to be
a conversation between kids.

111
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:22,020
This person behind you, I'm guessing
she's your magic item engineer?

112
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,600
Yup, that's right!

113
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,240
You see, she's the best around!

114
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:29,755
Whatever engineer you hired
can't hold a candle to her!

115
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:35,100
Well then, I'll let you keep up your
confident facade while you still can.

116
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:39,635
It'll only make the sight of your
miserable frustration all the sweeter.

117
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:45,017
She makes me so mad!

118
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:46,340
My apologies.

119
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:48,597
I'm sorry you had to
see all that ugliness.

120
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,092
Nah, it was actually pretty fun to watch.

121
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,070
Hello there.

122
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:56,017
Attention, ladies and gentlemen.

123
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,917
We welcome you to this year's event.

124
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,588
We will now begin the
unveiling festivities.

125
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:01,994
Our first participant.

126
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:06,433
If you would be so kind, what sort of
magic item did you bring to show us?

127
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:12,628
This magic item can transform
into a wide variety of weapons.

128
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:16,940
Oh, I theorized a similar concept
once. This should be good.

129
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,430
Ha!

130
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:26,277
Well, what do you think?

131
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,137
With this magic item's special ability,

132
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:30,337
you no longer have to carry
a ton of different weapons?

133
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,361
around with you.

134
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:38,040
Yeah, that reaction makes sense. Voila!

135
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,137
Is it our turn yet?

136
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,857
I want to get this over with.

137
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:49,397
This is the moment you've
all been waiting for.

138
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:52,127
We will now unveil Miss
Kanashi's magic item.

139
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,122
We hope you enjoy the spectacle.

140
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:02,444
I'm excited to show you the magic
item my engineer brought along.

141
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:04,072
Feast your eyes on this.

142
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:06,380
Let's see what you're so proud of.

143
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:09,625
Eh, whatever it is, I
doubt it's anything good.

144
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:20,920
This unique magic item was produced based
on the physiology of a certain monster.

145
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:24,440
Behold, it will obey any command I give.

146
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,718
Is that impossible?

147
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:27,080
Hold on, no.

148
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:32,251
To create an intelligent magic item has
long been a dream for all engineers.

149
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:35,755
And yet, I have accomplished
this nigh impossible feat.

150
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:42,170
Hey.

151
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,617
Remember what I said
when we got kidnapped?

152
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:48,977
With our current technology, there's no
way to give a magic item intelligence.

153
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:49,890
Hello there!

154
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:54,640
But if you put a person's soul
inside, it's not out of the question.

155
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,937
Though doing so is extremely
dangerous and was declared

156
00:09:58,020 --> 00:10:00,844
illegal by the Magic Item
Engineers Association.

157
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:04,537
Once, a foolish engineer
thought he was above this rule.

158
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:07,400
And his hubris destroyed an entire town.

159
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,078
Does that mean we're in danger here?

160
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:16,680
So, tell me, have you seen anything as
marvelous as this magic item before?

161
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:19,254
We know who this year's winner will be.

162
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,480
Must kill!

163
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:23,160
What's this?

164
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:26,380
You never mentioned it was
capable of human speech.

165
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:31,559
Shit, I was afraid something
like this would happen.

166
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:33,500
Must kill!

167
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:35,950
Must kill!

168
00:10:36,033 --> 00:10:37,477
Wait, what's going on here?

169
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:39,157
I didn't equip it with a speech function!

170
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,120
I have to shut it down!

171
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:43,480
This is you who helped me!

172
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,720
How dare you away from my slumber!

173
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:51,520
That idiot!

174
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:55,560
He forced a human soul inside
of that magic puppet! Hey, what?

175
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:56,840
I'm scared!

176
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,880
Hey, you! Shades!

177
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:02,200
Can you hold that thing down? Ma 'am!

178
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,080
This is it!

179
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:16,357
Here's the magic seal
keeping the soul in place!

180
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:18,852
They even put a brainwashing spell on it!

181
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,520
Have some respect for the dead, dammit!

182
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:23,260
Only way!

183
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:29,100
I'm sorry.

184
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,167
That must have been torture.

185
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,720
It's not your fault.

186
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:39,018
You were forced out of your slumber.

187
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:41,957
Something like this shouldn't
have happened to you.

188
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:45,800
I promise your rest won't
be disrupted again. No!

189
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,180
How can this be?

190
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:49,497
I devoted years to
creating that technique.

191
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:51,957
It was supposed to be
my life's greatest work.

192
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:54,300
How did you deactivate it so quickly?

193
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:57,857
You call that crude bit of
engineering your life's work?

194
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:59,060
What a joke.

195
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:03,809
With Hulemy on the case, that was easier
than squishing a frog fiend tadpole.

196
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,980
Wait, Hulemy?

197
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:07,857
You don't mean the girl
wonder of mayhem, Hulemy.

198
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:10,617
Wasn't she the problem child
at the center of all those

199
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:13,657
explosions and fires at the
school of magic item engineers?

200
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:16,577
One time she made a sleeping potion so
strong she put the whole school to sleep.

201
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:20,077
She made a water purifying drug,
but when she put it in a pond,

202
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:23,177
it ended up vaporizing the
water instead of purifying it.

203
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,090
You jerks!

204
00:12:24,173 --> 00:12:26,608
Why can't you let that
all stay in the past?

205
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,580
It's such a shame.

206
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:32,269
Looks like your magic item
engineer just wasn't good enough.

207
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:36,737
Oh brother, things got a
little hairy for a moment,

208
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:38,917
but everything turned
out all right in the end.

209
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,537
If you ask me, this
counts as a job well done.

210
00:12:41,620 --> 00:12:43,840
Well, I do have one minor complaint.

211
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:48,048
I get the feeling that everyone's
totally forgotten about me!

212
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,891
Lately, it started snowing in the village.

213
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:58,419
It seems that Winter has finally
come to the Clear Flow Lake Stratum.

214
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:04,600
Everyone, thank you for
gathering here today.

215
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:08,337
I never would have imagined their
reach would extend this far.

216
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:10,537
Yeah, I guess we got too complacent.

217
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:14,037
They've taken control of 70 % of
the strata they've been released in,

218
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:16,977
and now they've set their sights
on the Clear Flow Lake Stratum.

219
00:13:17,060 --> 00:13:20,097
We have to mount a counterattack,
otherwise we'll be ruined.

220
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:22,617
We must set aside our
differences and come together.

221
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:26,897
We will join hands in order to eliminate
the worst threat we've ever faced,

222
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:28,800
Chains Restaurant! Hear, hear!

223
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:31,257
At this rate, our
businesses will go under.

224
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:32,937
I'd rather die than lose my shop.

225
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:36,857
I've taken the liberty to invite a
certain someone to be our secret weapon.

226
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:40,140
Would you mind saying hello
to the group? Hello there!

227
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:43,520
Thank you for joining us today, Boxo.

228
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,992
Based on everything I've gathered so far,

229
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:51,397
it seems a big-time restaurant chain has
set its sights on our little village.

230
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:55,715
This chain's restaurant poses an
existential threat to local businesses.

231
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:57,000
I'll be frank.

232
00:13:57,220 --> 00:14:00,457
We've been driven into a corner and
we're running out of options here.

233
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,658
Damn that greedy chain's restaurant.

234
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,497
At this rate, I won't be
able to feed my children.

235
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:08,521
How are we supposed to
survive through the winter?

236
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:11,920
I know why they invited me today.

237
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:13,917
As ridiculous as it sounds,

238
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,717
they're expecting a
vending machine to figure

239
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,117
out a way to get them
out of this situation.

240
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:22,494
Please, Boxo, would you be willing to
lend us a hand through this crisis?

241
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:24,120
If you agree to help,

242
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:26,377
I promise to let Llamas
stay at the end for

243
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:28,337
half price once it's back up and running.

244
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:31,640
If it'll help Llamas out,
there's no way I'll refuse.

245
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:33,520
Hello there.

246
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,100
Thank you very much.

247
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:40,025
I'm glad everyone's excited, but
we're not out of the woods yet.

248
